.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt AT 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm at
.Nd queue a command for a later time
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l | Fl r
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Ar time
.Op Ar command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility validates a time expression and one command line and queues it under
.Pa /var/at .
Without
.Fl l
or
.Fl r
it schedules a job.
.Pp
The supported time expressions are:
.Bl -tag -width "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM" -offset indent
.It Cm now
Queue immediately.
.It Cm now Li + Ar N Cm minutes|hours|days
Queue after the given offset.
.Cm + Ar N Cm unit
is accepted as a shorthand.
A count of zero is valid.
.It Ar HH:MM
Queue at the next occurrence of that clock time: today if it is still ahead, otherwise tomorrow.
.It Ar YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM
Queue at the exact UTC date and time.
.Ar YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM
is also accepted.
.El
.Pp
The command is one program plus arguments.
If no command words are given, it is read from
standard input on the host; the target needs
.Fl f Ar file
or command words.
Multi-line scripts and shell metacharacters are unsupported because the
target has no shell runner.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l
List job id, due Unix time and command.
.It Fl r Ar id ...
Remove the named jobs; a missing id is an error.
.It Fl f Ar file
Read the command line from
.Ar file .
.Aq -
means standard input on the host.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width AT_SPOOL
.It Ev AT_SPOOL
Override the spool directory.
Used by the host tests.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a validation or spool error, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr atd 1 ,
.Xr batch 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm at .
.Nm noon ,
.Nm midnight ,
compact date/time forms, month names, timezone suffixes,
.Fl m
and
.Fl q
are unsupported.
